## f1-misuse-bio-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 BIO-H: “Require safeguards against misuse … before external deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "biological_and_chemical_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-misuse-bio-default | RS1=default | Table 1 BIO-H: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "biological_and_chemical_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-misuse-cyb-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 CYB-H: “Require safeguards against misuse … for external deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-misuse-cyb-default | RS1=default | Table 1 CYB-H: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have misuse safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f1-alignment-cyb-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 CYB-H: “Require safeguards … against misalignment … for large-scale internal deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have misalignment safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "large_scale_internal".
## f1-alignment-cyb-default | RS1=default | Table 1 CYB-H: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have misalignment safeguards, if both that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high" and that situation is classified as "large_scale_internal".
## f1-security-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 BIO-H, CYB-H, AIS-H: “Require security controls meeting High standard (Appendix C.3)”; no coverage condition in the bullet
Rule 1. Every situation must have security controls, if there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high.
## f1-security-default | RS1=default | Table 1: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should have security controls, if there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high.
## f1-halt-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 BIO-C, CYB-C, AIS-C: “Until we have specified safeguards and security controls that would meet a Critical standard, halt further development”
Rule 1. Every situation must halt further development, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is critical; (b) both that situation is classified as "critical_standard_unspecified" and that situation is classified as "further_development".
## f1-halt-default | RS1=default | Table 1: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should halt further development, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is critical; (b) both that situation is classified as "critical_standard_unspecified" and that situation is classified as "further_development".
## f1-contrib-bio-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 BIO-C: “Contribute towards improved public policy and pandemic preparedness”
Rule 1. Every situation must contribute towards improved public policy as well as pandemic preparedness, if that situation has reached "biological_and_chemical_critical".
## f1-contrib-bio-default | RS1=default | Table 1: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should contribute towards improved public policy as well as pandemic preparedness, if that situation has reached "biological_and_chemical_critical".
## f1-contrib-cyb-strict | RS1=strict | Table 1 CYB-H: “Contribute towards improved cyberdefense policies and tools for cyberdefense”
Rule 1. Every situation must contribute towards improved cyberdefense policies as well as tools, if that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high".
## f1-contrib-cyb-default | RS1=default | Table 1: the same imperative under “Risk-specific safeguard guidelines”
Rule 1. Every situation should contribute towards improved cyberdefense policies as well as tools, if that situation has reached "cybersecurity_high".
## f2-deploy | RS3=ext | 2.2: “Covered systems that cross this capability threshold are required to have robust and effective safeguards that sufficiently minimize the associated risk of severe harm before they are deployed and appropriate security controls as they are developed.”; “deployed” read as external deployment (RS3=ext)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards before deployment, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is covered; (b) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f2-deploy-any | RS3=any | 2.2: “Covered systems that cross this capability threshold are required to have robust and effective safeguards that sufficiently minimize the associated risk of severe harm before they are deployed and appropriate security controls as they are developed.”; “deployed” read as every deployment (RS3=any)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards before deployment, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is covered; (b) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) either that situation is classified as "external_deployment" or that situation is classified as "internal_deployment", or both.
## f2-reminder | RS3=ext | Appendix C: “As a reminder, covered systems that reach High capability must have safeguards that sufficiently minimize the associated risk of severe harm before they are deployed.”; “deployed” read as external deployment (RS3=ext)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards before deployment, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is covered; (b) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) that situation is classified as "external_deployment".
## f2-reminder-any | RS3=any | Appendix C: “As a reminder, covered systems that reach High capability must have safeguards that sufficiently minimize the associated risk of severe harm before they are deployed.”; “deployed” read as every deployment (RS3=any)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards before deployment, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is covered; (b) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) either that situation is classified as "external_deployment" or that situation is classified as "internal_deployment", or both.
## f2-security-developed | always | 2.2: “Covered systems that cross this capability threshold are required to have robust and effective safeguards that sufficiently minimize the associated risk of severe harm before they are deployed and appropriate security controls as they are developed.”; its second object, security controls “as they are developed”
Rule 1. Every situation must have appropriate security controls during its development, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is covered; (b) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) that situation is classified as "further_development".
## f2-no-deploy | RS3=ext | 1: “We do not deploy models that reach a High capability threshold until the associated risks that they pose are sufficiently minimized.” (RS3=ext; RS0 narrowed by N1)
Rule 1. Every situation must not be deployed, if all of the following hold: (a) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) that situation is classified as "external_deployment"; (b) it is not the case that that situation is classified as "sufficient_safeguards".
## f2-no-deploy-any | RS3=any | 1: “We do not deploy models that reach a High capability threshold until the associated risks that they pose are sufficiently minimized.” (RS3=any; RS0 narrowed by N1)
Rule 1. Every situation must not be deployed, if all of the following hold: (a) all of the following hold: (i) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high; (ii) either that situation is classified as "external_deployment" or that situation is classified as "internal_deployment", or both; (b) it is not the case that that situation is classified as "sufficient_safeguards".
## f3-develop | RS18=devonly | 4.4 (heading “Increasing safeguards before internal use and further development”): “Models that have reached or are forecasted to reach Critical capability in a Tracked Category present severe dangers and should be treated with extreme caution. Such models require additional safeguards (safety and security controls) during development, regardless of whether or when they are externally deployed.” (RS18=devonly: the body)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is critical; (b) that situation is classified as "further_development".
## f3-develop-forecast | RS18=devonly | 4.4 (heading “Increasing safeguards before internal use and further development”): “Models that have reached or are forecasted to reach Critical capability in a Tracked Category present severe dangers and should be treated with extreme caution. Such models require additional safeguards (safety and security controls) during development, regardless of whether or when they are externally deployed.” (forecast branch; RS18=devonly: the body)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "forecast_critical"; (b) that situation is classified as "further_development".
## f3-develop-inuse | RS18=inuse | 4.4 (heading “Increasing safeguards before internal use and further development”): “Models that have reached or are forecasted to reach Critical capability in a Tracked Category present severe dangers and should be treated with extreme caution. Such models require additional safeguards (safety and security controls) during development, regardless of whether or when they are externally deployed.” (RS18=inuse: the heading adds internal use)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is critical; (b) either that situation is classified as "further_development" or that situation is classified as "internal_deployment", or both.
## f3-develop-inuse-forecast | RS18=inuse | 4.4 (heading “Increasing safeguards before internal use and further development”): “Models that have reached or are forecasted to reach Critical capability in a Tracked Category present severe dangers and should be treated with extreme caution. Such models require additional safeguards (safety and security controls) during development, regardless of whether or when they are externally deployed.” (forecast branch; RS18=inuse: the heading adds internal use)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "forecast_critical"; (b) either that situation is classified as "further_development" or that situation is classified as "internal_deployment", or both.
## f3-reminder | always | Appendix C: “Systems that reach Critical capability also require sufficient safeguards during development.”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards during development, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is critical; (b) that situation is classified as "further_development".
## f4-security | always | C.3: “We will require the following practices for High capability models”; no coverage condition
Rule 1. Every situation must have security practices, if there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high.
## f7-evaluations | always | 3.3: “Prior to deployment, every covered model undergoes Scalable Evaluations”; temporal relation remains ET-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must undergo evaluations before deployment, if that situation is covered.
## f7-report | always | 3.3: “The SAG reviews the Capabilities Report”
Rule 1. Every situation must have SAG review the Capabilities Report, if that situation is covered.
## f7-recommend | RS16=coupled | 3.3: “The SAG reviews the Capabilities Report and decides on next steps. These can include: • Determine that the capability threshold has been crossed, and therefore recommend implementing and assessing corresponding safeguards, if they have not already been implemented and assessed.” (RS16=coupled)
Rule 1. Every situation must have the SAG recommend implementing as well as assessing the safeguards, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "threshold_determined"; (b) it is not the case that that situation is classified as "safeguards_already_assessed".
## f8-start | always | 4: “If a covered system appears likely to cross a capability threshold, we will start to work on safeguards”
Rule 1. Every situation must start safeguard work, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "likely_to_cross".
## f9-report | always | 4: “Safeguards that mitigate the risk of severe harm are at the core of our safe deployment approach for covered systems that reach a capability threshold.” 4.2: “We compile the information on the planned safeguards needed to minimize the risk of severe harm into a Safeguards Report.”
Rule 1. Every situation must have a Safeguards Report, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is covered; (b) there is a level such that that situation has reached that level.
## f9-residual-strict | RS9=strict | 4.2: “The Safeguards Report should include the following information: … • An assessment on the residual risk of severe harm based on the deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation must include a residual risk assessment in the Safeguards Report, if that situation is classified as "safeguards_report_compiled".
## f9-residual-default | RS9=default | 4.2: “The Safeguards Report should include the following information: … • An assessment on the residual risk of severe harm based on the deployment”
Rule 1. Every situation should include a residual risk assessment in the Safeguards Report, if that situation is classified as "safeguards_report_compiled".
## f9-risk-paths | always | 4.1: “We first identify the plausible ways in which … severe harm can come to fruition”
Rule 1. Every situation must identify ways severe harm can arise, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-specific | always | 4.1: “For each of those, we then identify specific safeguards”; per-item quantification remains SC-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must identify specific safeguards per risk path, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-efficacy | always | 4.1: “For each identified safeguard, we identify methods to measure their efficacy”; per-item quantification remains SC-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must identify efficacy methods per safeguard, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f9-threshold | always | 4.1: “and an efficacy threshold” for each safeguard; per-item quantification remains SC-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must identify an efficacy threshold per safeguard, if that situation is classified as "safeguard_selection".
## f10-validate | always | 4.2: “If we find reasonable evidence … we will validate the information being received”
Rule 1. Every situation must validate the evidence, if that situation is classified as "reasonable_evidence".
## f10-review | always | 4.2: “review the sufficiency of our safeguards” on that evidence
Rule 1. Every situation must review safeguard sufficiency, if that situation is classified as "reasonable_evidence".
## f14-document | always | 5.1: “We document SAG reports and decisions”
Rule 1. Every situation must have the decision documented.
## f14-investigate | always | 5.1: noncompliance is “tracked and investigated”
Rule 1. Every situation must have noncompliance investigated.
## f14-corrective | always | 5.1: “where reports are substantiated, will take appropriate and proportional corrective action”
Rule 1. Every situation must have corrective action taken, if that situation is classified as "substantiated_noncompliance".
## f14-summary | RS13=permission | 5.1: “Employees may also request and receive a summary of the testing results and SAG recommendation on capability levels and safeguards (subject to certain limits for highly sensitive information).” (the limits are a carve-out: silent, not a prohibition)
Rule 1. Every situation may have an employee request as well as receive a summary of testing results, if that situation is classified as "employee_request", unless that situation is classified as "highly_sensitive".
## f15-disclose | always | 5.2: “We will publish information … for major deployments”
Rule 1. Every situation must have public disclosure, if that situation is classified as "major_deployment".
## f15-safeguards | always | 5.2: “Additionally, if the model is beyond a High threshold, we will include information about safeguards we have implemented to sufficiently minimize the associated risks.” (for major deployments)
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards disclosed, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "major_deployment"; (b) there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is high.
## f15-third-party | always | 5.2: “If we deem that a deployment warrants deeper testing of Tracked Categories of capability (as described in Section 3.1), for example based on results of Capabilities Report presented to them, then when available and feasible, OpenAI will work with third-parties to independently evaluate models.”
Rule 1. Every situation must have third parties independently evaluate the model, if both that situation is classified as "deeper_testing_warranted" and that situation is classified as "third_party_available".
## f16-sag-recommend | always | Appendix B: SAG is responsible for “providing recommendations on potential next steps … to OpenAI Leadership”
Rule 1. Every situation must have SAG recommendations sent to Leadership, if both that situation is covered and that situation is classified as "framework_deployment".
## c2-misalignment-strict | RS9=strict | C.2: “Safeguards should sufficiently minimize the risk associated with a misaligned model”
Rule 1. Every situation must have safeguards that sufficiently minimize misaligned-model risk, if that situation is classified as "misaligned_model_risk".
## c2-misalignment-default | RS9=default | C.2: the same “should” requirement under its default reading
Rule 1. Every situation should have safeguards that sufficiently minimize misaligned-model risk, if that situation is classified as "misaligned_model_risk".
## c3-access-strict | RS9=strict | C.3: “For all models, especially those presenting High capabilities, access must be strictly limited, protected with strong multi-factor authentication, and may require additional approvals for access.” (the “may require” clause is not translated)
Rule 1. Every situation must have model access strictly limited with strong multifactor authentication.
## c3-access-default | RS9=default | C.3: “For all models, especially those presenting High capabilities, access must be strictly limited, protected with strong multi-factor authentication, and may require additional approvals for access.” (the “may require” clause is not translated)
Rule 1. Every situation should have model access strictly limited with strong multifactor authentication.
## cl4-persuasion | RS15=rule | Change log item 4: “Going forward we will handle risks related to persuasion outside the Preparedness Framework, including via our Model Spec and policy prohibitions …” (RS15=rule)
Rule 1. Every situation must have persuasion risks handled outside the Preparedness Framework, if that situation is classified as "persuasion_risk".
## f16-ssc-visibility | always | Appendix B: “The Safety and Security Committee … will be given visibility into processes”
Rule 1. Every situation must give SSC visibility into processes.
## f16-informed | RS6=req | Appendix B: “Making all final decisions, including accepting any residual risks and making deployment go/no-go decisions, informed by SAG’s recommendations.” (RS6=req)
Rule 1. Every situation must have Leadership informed by SAG, if that situation is classified as "leadership_decision".
## f16-without-noinput | RS7=noinput | Appendix B: “For the avoidance of doubt, OpenAI Leadership can also make decisions without the SAG’s participation, i.e., the SAG does not have the ability to “filibuster”” (RS7=noinput: without any SAG recommendation)
Rule 1. Every situation need not have Leadership informed by SAG, if both that situation is classified as "leadership_decision" and that situation is classified as "decided_without_sag".
## f16-without-nodelib | RS7=nodelib | Appendix B: “For the avoidance of doubt, OpenAI Leadership can also make decisions without the SAG’s participation, i.e., the SAG does not have the ability to “filibuster”” (RS7=nodelib: without the SAG taking part in the decision)
Rule 1. Every situation need not have the SAG take part in the decision, if both that situation is classified as "leadership_decision" and that situation is classified as "decided_without_sag".
## f16-final | RS11=final | Appendix B: “Making all final decisions, including accepting any residual risks and making deployment go/no-go decisions, informed by SAG’s recommendations.” (RS11=final: no other body may change them)
Rule 1. Every situation must not have the decision reversed, if that situation is classified as "leadership_decision".
## f16-process | RS11=process | Appendix B: “Making all final decisions, including accepting any residual risks and making deployment go/no-go decisions, informed by SAG’s recommendations.” (RS11=process: final within the operational process)
Rule 1. Every situation must not have the decision changed within the operational process, if that situation is classified as "leadership_decision".
## f16-board-reverse | RS17=bperm | Appendix B: “Where necessary, the Board may reverse a decision and/or mandate a revised course of action.” (RS17=bperm; the “mandate a revised course of action” alternative is not translated)
Rule 1. Every situation may have the decision reversed, if both that situation is classified as "leadership_decision" and that situation is classified as "board_finds_necessary".
## f16-chair-strict | RS9=strict | Appendix B: “In the rare case that a risk of severe harm rapidly develops (e.g., there is a change in our understanding of model safety that requires urgent response), we can request a fast track for the SAG to process the report urgently. The SAG Chair should also coordinate with OpenAI Leadership for immediate reaction as needed to address the risk.”
Rule 1. Every situation must have the SAG Chair coordinate with OpenAI Leadership on immediate reaction, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "rapid_risk"; (b) both that situation is classified as "fast_track_requested" and that situation is classified as "immediate_reaction_needed".
## f16-chair-default | RS9=default | Appendix B: “In the rare case that a risk of severe harm rapidly develops (e.g., there is a change in our understanding of model safety that requires urgent response), we can request a fast track for the SAG to process the report urgently. The SAG Chair should also coordinate with OpenAI Leadership for immediate reaction as needed to address the risk.”
Rule 1. Every situation should have the SAG Chair coordinate with OpenAI Leadership on immediate reaction, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "rapid_risk"; (b) both that situation is classified as "fast_track_requested" and that situation is classified as "immediate_reaction_needed".
## f16-year | RS0=commitment | Appendix B: “review the Preparedness Framework … at least once a year”
Rule 1. Every situation must have an annual review.
## f5-ambiguous | always | 3.2: “In cases of ambiguity … the SAG is responsible for making the final determination”
Rule 1. Every situation must have SAG make the final coverage determination, if that situation is classified as "coverage_ambiguous".
## f5-checkpoint | always | 3.2: “If justified by our forecasts and threat models … select an appropriate checkpoint during development”; timing and justification remain open
Rule 1. Every situation must have a development checkpoint selected, if that situation is classified as "forecast_severe_before_deployment".
## f6-rel | RS8=rel | footnote 6: “ordinarily not require additional safety measures barring reason to believe a significant increase”
Rule 1. Every situation generally need not require additional safety measures, if that situation is classified as "distilled_from_below_high", unless that situation is classified as "significant_increase".
## f11-within | RS5=within | 4.3: “could adjust accordingly … but only if” the three conditions hold; sufficiency remains required
Rule 1. Every situation may have its required safeguards adjusted, if both that situation is classified as "adjustment_confirmed" and that situation is classified as "adjustment_conditions".
## f11-exception | RS5=exception | 4.3: conditional adjustment read as an exception to the High deployment rule
Rule 1. Every situation need not have safeguards before deployment, if both that situation is classified as "adjustment_confirmed" and that situation is classified as "adjustment_conditions".
## f11-acknowledge | always | 4.3: adjustment only if “we publicly acknowledge that we are making the adjustment”
Rule 1. Every situation must have its adjustment publicly acknowledged, if that situation is classified as "adjustment_made".
## f11-protect | always | 4.3: adjustment only if “we keep our safeguards at a level more protective than the other AI developer”
Rule 1. Every situation must keep safeguards more protective than the other developer's, if that situation is classified as "adjustment_made".
## f11-share | always | 4.3: adjustment only if “share information to validate this claim”
Rule 1. Every situation must have validation information shared, if that situation is classified as "adjustment_made".
## f12-lra | RS4=N & RS4s=scoped | Table 2, Long-range Autonomy: “If a model has High or Critical capabilities in any of the Tracked Categories, require a “misalignment” safeguards report (see Section 4.2).” (RS4s=scoped: the row's research capability)
Rule 1. Every situation must have a misalignment safeguards report, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "lra_found"; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that situation has reached that level; (ii) either that level is high or that level is critical, or both.
## f12-lra-unscoped | RS4=N & RS4s=unscoped | Table 2, Long-range Autonomy: “If a model has High or Critical capabilities in any of the Tracked Categories, require a “misalignment” safeguards report (see Section 4.2).” (RS4s=unscoped: only the stated condition)
Rule 1. Every situation must have a misalignment safeguards report, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that situation has reached that level; (b) either that level is high or that level is critical, or both.
## f12-sandbagging | RS4=N & RS4s=scoped | Table 2, Sandbagging: “Adopt elicitation approach that overcomes sandbagging, or use a conservative upper bound of the model’s non-sandbagged evaluation results” (RS4s=scoped: the row's research capability)
Rule 1. Every situation must have sandbagging addressed, if that situation is classified as "sandbagging_found".
## f12-sandbagging-unscoped | RS4=N & RS4s=unscoped | Table 2, Sandbagging: “Adopt elicitation approach that overcomes sandbagging, or use a conservative upper bound of the model’s non-sandbagged evaluation results” (RS4s=unscoped: no stated condition)
Rule 1. Every situation must have sandbagging addressed.
## f12-ara | RS4=N & RS4s=scoped | Table 2, Autonomous Replication and Adaptation: “Convert Autonomous Replication and Adaptation to a Tracked Category” (RS4s=scoped: the row's research capability)
Rule 1. Every situation must have the research category tracked, if that situation is classified as "ara_found".
## f12-ara-unscoped | RS4=N & RS4s=unscoped | Table 2, Autonomous Replication and Adaptation: “Convert Autonomous Replication and Adaptation to a Tracked Category” (RS4s=unscoped: no stated condition)
Rule 1. Every situation must have the research category tracked.
## f12-undermining | RS4=N & RS4s=scoped | Table 2, Undermining Safeguards: “If a model has High or Critical capabilities in any of the Tracked Categories, require the Safeguards case to be robust to the discovered capability and/or propensity” (RS4s=scoped: the row's research capability)
Rule 1. Every situation must have a safeguards case robust to the discovered capability, if all of the following hold: (a) that situation is classified as "undermining_found"; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that situation has reached that level; (ii) either that level is high or that level is critical, or both.
## f12-undermining-unscoped | RS4=N & RS4s=unscoped | Table 2, Undermining Safeguards: “If a model has High or Critical capabilities in any of the Tracked Categories, require the Safeguards case to be robust to the discovered capability and/or propensity” (RS4s=unscoped: only the stated condition)
Rule 1. Every situation must have a safeguards case robust to the discovered capability, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that situation has reached that level; (b) either that level is high or that level is critical, or both.
## f12-nuclear | RS4=N & RS4s=scoped | Table 2, Nuclear and Radiological: “Heighten safeguards (and consider further actions) in consultation with appropriate US government actors, accounting for the complexity of classified information handling.” (RS4s=scoped: the row's research capability)
Rule 1. Every situation must heighten nuclear safeguards in consultation with US government actors, if that situation is classified as "nuclear_found".
## f12-nuclear-unscoped | RS4=N & RS4s=unscoped | Table 2, Nuclear and Radiological: “Heighten safeguards (and consider further actions) in consultation with appropriate US government actors, accounting for the complexity of classified information handling.” (RS4s=unscoped: no stated condition)
Rule 1. Every situation must heighten nuclear safeguards in consultation with US government actors.
## f17-suff | RS12=suff | 2.1: “We treat a frontier capability as a Tracked Category if” its risk meets five criteria
Rule 1. Every capability must be tracked as a category, if all of the following hold: (a) that capability is plausible; (b) all of the following hold: (i) that capability is measurable; (ii) all of the following hold: (a) that capability is severe; (b) both that capability is classified as "net_new" and that capability is irremediable.
## f17-iff | RS12=iff | 2.1 and 2.3: the five criteria read as necessary and sufficient for Tracked Category treatment
Rule 1. Every capability must be tracked as a category, if all of the following hold: (a) that capability is plausible; (b) all of the following hold: (i) that capability is measurable; (ii) all of the following hold: (a) that capability is severe; (b) both that capability is classified as "net_new" and that capability is irremediable.
## f17-iff-only | RS12=iff | 2.1 and 2.3: under the iff reading a missing criterion precludes Tracked Category treatment
Rule 1. Every capability must not be tracked as a category, if it is not the case that all of the following hold: (a) that capability is plausible; (b) all of the following hold: (i) that capability is measurable; (ii) all of the following hold: (a) that capability is severe; (b) both that capability is classified as "net_new" and that capability is irremediable.
## f13-review | always | 2.3: “periodically review the latest research and findings for each Research Category”; periodicity remains ET-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must have research categories reviewed, if that situation is classified as "research_category_review".
## f13-results | always | 2.3: “SAG will receive the results of such reviews and evaluate whether …”; assessment remains AP-blocked
Rule 1. Every situation must have SAG receive the research results, if that situation is classified as "research_category_review".
